INT. VERONA GARDEN CENTER - GREENHOUSE - DAY

Humid. Rows of potted ferns and trays of seedlings. A hand-painted sign: "WEDDING SEASON SALE!" Dust motes in the sun through fogged glass.

LUCIA ROSSI, 30s, in a green apron, lifts a tray of orchids. MATTEO BELLINI, 30s, in a suit, stands frozen with a bouquet of white roses. GWEN PRITCHARD, 30s, Matteo's fiancee, wears a sundress and sunglasses on her head. DEV MALHOTRA, 30s, Lucia's ex, leans against a potting bench. AUNT FABIOLA, 70s, in a floral housecoat, supervises from a folding chair. STAN, 50s, the garden center owner, holds a hose and a clipboard.

MATTEO
Lucia.

LUCIA
Matteo.

GWEN
(brightly)
You two know each other?

DEV
Know is a strong word.

AUNT FABIOLA
They were engaged. Eight years ago. She threw a plate at him.

LUCIA
It was a saucer.

STAN
Folks, I've got a delivery of mulch at two. Can we speed this up?

GWEN
Matteo, why didn't you tell me?

MATTEO
I didn't think it mattered.

DEV
It matters.

LUCIA
Dev, stay out of it.

DEV
I'm standing in it.

AUNT FABIOLA
Stan, hose them.

STAN
I'm not hosing customers.

GWEN
I want the white roses. Just the roses.

LUCIA
They're not for sale.

GWEN
I'm the customer.

LUCIA
They're mine. I grew them.

MATTEO
Lucia, the wedding is Saturday.

LUCIA
Then you'd better pick another florist.

DEV
Or another bride.

Gwen takes off her sunglasses, slowly.

GWEN
Say that again.

DEV
I said --

AUNT FABIOLA
Enough! This is a greenhouse, not a telenovela.

STAN
Actually, ma'am, the ficus are getting stressed.

Lucia sets down the orchids. Matteo steps toward her, and the roses fall from his hands.

MATTEO
I never stopped.

GWEN
Matteo!

LUCIA
Don't.

DEV
(under his breath)
Finally.

Aunt Fabiola reaches into her housecoat, draws out a saucer, and holds it up like a trophy.
